# i18n Required for UI Copy

- Never hardcode user-facing UI text in Vue components, composables, or utility data files.
- All user-visible labels, titles, descriptions, helper text, aria text, button copy, and empty-state text must come from i18n keys.
- When adding new UI copy, add keys for `en`, `zh`, `es`, and `nl` locale files in `i18n/locales/`.
- In data-only files like `app/utils/markdownExamples.ts`, keep structural IDs and content snippets only; localized display text must be resolved through i18n at render time.
- If a new feature ships with missing translations, treat it as incomplete and add locale entries before finalizing.
